{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Did I not also send to your messengers</b> — Balaam now excuses himself with what he said to Balak's messengers when they returned to him, before he knew what YHWH would further speak with him. But after that, he showed that he would come and curse, until the angel warned him on the way, as I have explained (Ramban on Numbers 22:20)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The lemma 'הֲלֹא גַּם אֶל מַלְאָכֶיךָ' corresponds to the phrase in Numbers 24:12; the argument is that Balaam deflects blame by citing what he had told the messengers earlier."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:18.306905699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}